.TH CSTRING_SUBSTRING 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_substring \- create a new string from a sub-range
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cstring.h>

cstr cstring_substring(cstr s, size_t start, size_t length, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocates a new cstring containing characters in the range
[start, start + length). If start + length extends beyond the end of the
string the range is clamped to the actual end. If start is at or beyond
the string length an empty cstring is returned.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s        Source string
start    Zero-based start index
length   Number of characters to include
err      Optional pointer to receive an error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
New cstring on success
NULL on allocation failure (details written to *err if err is non-NULL)
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Caller must destroy the returned cstring when done
The range is clamped rather than rejected when it extends past the end
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_copy (3),
.BR cstring_split (3),
.BR cstring_find (3)
